* '''Mod Goblin:''' Tombs of Amascut is likely the most accessible raid (and I think Chambers of Xeric in a group is pretty accessible anyway) and then the difficulty for Tombs of Amascut comes from the invocations, etc. 
* '''Mod Goblin:''' I'm hoping you'll be pleasantly surprised by the accessibility of Tombs of Amascut. Also in regards to expecting a new generation of players to perform like the older players, I think the average RuneScape player now, especially since ToB, the average PvMer is so many leagues better than the average PvMer before ToB’s release. Obviously newer players have to learn certain things, however the resources to learn from are far better now.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' I think overall Tombs of Amascut will be able to be engaged with by far more people than this question asker realises. Tombs of Amascut scales to be easier than Chambers all the way up to be harder than ToB.
* '''Mod Sarnie:'''  Especially with ToB specifically, I know the rewards are less but there is an entry mode if you want to try an easier version of ToB. It is an amazing entryway into learning how to PvM.
* '''Mod Goblin:''' You could always have your colleagues carry you through it for a Quest Cape, isn’t that right Mod Sarnie? 
* '''Mod Sarnie:''' Don’t call me out like that!

